Let's consider special summon UI and AI carefully.

AI:
- Before normal summon, check if it can special summon VD11. The AI hand might have VD11, own monsters >=1, empty zone. Should it? VD11's ATK decreases by released DEF, cannot be destroyed by battle, redirects damage. It's generally good if released monster DEF low. Score: base 2011 - releasedDef. If releasedDef <= maybe 1000, ATK 1011+. It's indestructible and redirects damage, so even 0 ATK is a good wall? But it's in atk position; if it attacks and loses, damage redirects. It can attack every turn. AI can use it. But releasing a monster costs board presence. We can implement AI special summon when:
