Oops, I used `${esc(note)}` in a template string inside JS. `esc` is imported at top of duel-render? Yes, imported `esc`. Good. But the note is a template string like "リリース1体 → 特殊召喚"; esc returns string. Fine.

But wait: `btn` disabled based on check.ok. `check.reason` may be undefined if ok false? canSpecialSummon always returns reason. Good.

Now `onTrayClick` add case 'special'. In ui-duel.js. Also handle zone release selection and doDrop special, runEngine special.

Let's edit ui-duel.js.

First handleZone: Add special branch near top after entry computed and after attackReady? The attackReady branch is for field selection. For hand special action, we should handle before canDropOn. Place after attackReady block and before canDropOn.

```js
  if (app.sel?.type === 'hand' && app.sel.action === 'special') {
    const ownMonster = side === 'you' && entry && !entry.faceDown && (kind === 'monster' || (kind === 'emz' && entry.owner === 'you'));
    if (ownMonster) {
      app.sel.release = { kind, idx };
      sfx('select');
      toast(`${entry.card.name} をリリース（DEF ${d.defOf('you', entry)}）`, 'gold');
      renderDuel();
      return;
    }
    if (side === 'you' && kind === 'monster' && !entry) {
      if (!app.sel.release) { toast('先にリリースするモンスターを選択', 'bad'); return; }
      doDrop('monster', idx);
      return;
    }
    if (side === 'opp' || (side === 'you' && entry && !ownMonster)) {
      // fall through? If clicking spell zone, maybe ignore.
      toast('リリースできるのは自分の表側モンスターです', 'bad');
      return;
    }
  }
```
But `entry` for emz is `d.emz[idx]` (could be opponent's). `ownMonster` condition requires entry.owner === 'you'. Good.
When clicking empty monster zone with no release, we toast. But if user clicks empty zone before selecting release, maybe they intend zone selection; we require release first. Fine.
When clicking own set monster (faceDown), not allowed; toast. Good.
When clicking own spell/trap zone, `entry` may exist; toast. If empty spell zone, no entry and kind !== monster, the branch falls through to app.sel reset (below) which would clear selection. Better handle: if kind !== 'monster' and not release candidate, toast and return. Add a final else in special branch:
```js
    if (side === 'you' && kind === 'monster' && !entry) {...}
    toast('リリースするモンスター、または空きモンスターゾーンを選択', 'bad');
    return;
```
But clicking opponent monster while special action would toast. Fine.

However, clicking own field spell or emz? Emz own monster is releaseable. Field spell is not. Toast.

Then `canDropOn` handles empty monster zone when release set. But our special branch intercepts empty monster zone and calls doDrop directly, so canDropOn not needed. Good.

Do we need to allow clicking empty zone if release set but `canDropOn` false because zone occupied? Our branch checks `!entry`. Good.

Then `doDrop`:
```js
if (sel.type === 'hand' && sel.action === 'special') {
  if (!sel.release) return;
  perform({ type:'special', uid: sel.uid, zone: idx, releaseKind: sel.release.kind, releaseIdx: sel.release.idx });
  return;
}
```
before monster check.

`onTrayClick` case 'special':
```js
case 'special':
  if (sel?.type === 'hand' && sel.card.specialSummon) {
    const check = d.canSpecialSummon('you', sel.uid);
    if (!check.ok) { toast(check.reason, 'bad'); break; }
    sel.action = 'special';
    sel.release = null;
    sfx('select');
    renderDuel();
    toast('リリースする自分のモンスターを選択', 'gold');
  }
  break;
```
Also if user clicks 'special' from hand while sel already action? Tray changes. Fine.

`runEngine` case:
```js
case 'special': return d.specialSummon(side, action.uid, action.zone, { kind: action.releaseKind, idx: action.releaseIdx });
```

Also in `handleZone`, the existing `if (side === 'you' && app.sel && canDropOn('you', kind, idx))` after special branch will still work for normal. Fine.

One nuance: when sel.action === 'special' and user clicks own release monster, `entry` could be the VD11? No VD11 in hand. Fine.

