content.text:
Need to ensure `d.canSpecialSummon` is available in tray. Yes engine.

Now AI changes:
- Exclude special-only from normal summon.
- Add special summon before normal summon (or after extra?). The AI should release a monster. Add step 1.5 maybe after extra.
- Attack uses `atkForAttack`.
- Attack scoring for redirect/indestructible.

Let's edit ai.js.

Add helper:
```js
function specialSummonAction(duel, side, own, hand) {
  const card = hand.find(c => c.kind==='monster' && c.specialSummon);
  if (!card) return null;
  const zone = emptyZone(...);
  if (zone < 0) return null;
  const check = duel.canSpecialSummon(side, card.uid);
  if (!check.ok) return null;
  const release = own.slice().sort((a,b)=>duel.defOf(side,a.entry)-duel.defOf(side,b.entry))[0];
  if (!release) return null;
  const releasedDef = duel.defOf(side, release.entry);
  // don't sacrifice a strong board or a high-DEF wall for a weakened VD11
  if (own.length < 2) return null;
  if (releasedDef > 1200) return null;
  return {type:'special', uid: card.uid, zone, releaseKind: release.kind, releaseIdx: release.idx};
}
```
Why own.length < 2? If only one monster, releasing leaves VD11; might still be good but conservative. If own.length >=2 and releasedDef <= 1200, good. But if own.length=1 and the monster is a weak 800 DEF imp, VD11 1211 ATK indestructible is an upgrade; should allow. Maybe condition: `if (own.length < 2 && releasedDef > 800) return null;` and `if (releasedDef > 1400) return null;`. Let's think. AI has own monsters maybe 1 with DEF 1200; releasing gives VD11 ATK 811 but indestructible and redirects damage. It can still attack and redirect. It's arguably fine. But losing board presence? VD11 replaces it. So allow if releasedDef <= 1400. If own.length >=2, allow <= 1800? Releasing a 2200 DEF guardian gives ATK 0 but indestructible; not great. Let's use:
- if releasedDef > 1200 return null
- if own.length < 2 && releasedDef > 800 return null
This is conservative.

But if AI never gets VD11 due to deck (flame/gear), it will sometimes. Good.

Also AI needs to know `specialSummon` cards cannot be normal summoned; filter.

Attack scoring:
```js
const atk = duel.atkForAttack(side, a.entry);
...
const aImmune = !!a.entry.card.battle?.indestructible;
const aRedirect = !!a.entry.card.battle?.redirectDamage;
...
if (t.entry.faceDown || t.entry.position === 'def') {
  if (atk > tDef) score = 520 + atk*0.1;
  else score = aImmune ? 300 + (tDef - atk)*0.5 : -200 - (tDef - atk);
} else {
  diff...
  if (diff > 0) ...
  else if (diff === 0) score = aImmune ? 400 : ...
  else score = aImmune ? 250 + (-diff)*0.5 : -400 + diff;
}
if (aRedirect) score += 40;
```
Careful: if attacker is immune but target also immune? Not relevant for AI's own VD11. If aImmune, it won't be destroyed, and damage to it redirects. If it loses, opponent takes damage, so score positive. Good.
